{
  "question_id": "q_001_sql_histogram_tweets",
  "slug": "sql-histogram-tweets",
  "title": "Histogram of Tweets",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "company": "Twitter",
  "premium": false,
  "question": "Twitter data infrastructure engineers analyze tweet distribution histograms across the user base for the year 2022.\n\nA tweet histogram groups users by the total number of tweets they published in 2022, and counts how many users fall into each tweet frequency bucket.\n\nWrite a query to calculate the tweet histogram. Output the tweet bucket (`tweet_bucket`, representing number of tweets posted) and the count of users in that bucket (`users_num`), ordered by `tweet_bucket` in ascending order.",
  "notes": [
    "Based on the example output, there are two users who posted only one tweet in 2022, and one user who posted two tweets in 2022. The query groups the users by the number of tweets they posted and displays the number of users in each group."
  ],
  "tables": [
    {
      "table_name": "tweets",
      "columns": [
        {
          "column_name": "tweet_id",
          "data_type": "INT"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "user_id",
          "data_type": "INT"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "msg",
          "data_type": "VARCHAR(255)"
        },
        {
          "column_name": "tweet_date",
          "data_type": "DATETIME"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "sample_data": {
    "tweets": [
      {
        "tweet_id": "214252",
        "user_id": "111",
        "msg": "Am considering taking Tesla private at $420. Funding secured.",
        "tweet_date": "12/30/2021 00:00:00"
      },
      {
        "tweet_id": "739252",
        "user_id": "111",
        "msg": "Despite the constant negative press covfefe",
        "tweet_date": "01/01/2022 00:00:00"
      },
      {
        "tweet_id": "846402",
        "user_id": "111",
        "msg": "Excited to learn advanced SQL window functions today!",
        "tweet_date": "02/14/2022 00:00:00"
      },
      {
        "tweet_id": "241425",
        "user_id": "254",
        "msg": "If the salary is so competitive why won’t you tell me what it is?",
        "tweet_date": "03/01/2022 00:00:00"
      },
      {
        "tweet_id": "231574",
        "user_id": "148",
        "msg": "I no longer have a manager. I can't be managed",
        "tweet_date": "03/23/2022 00:00:00"
      }
    ]
  },
  "sample_output": [
    {
      "tweet_bucket": 1,
      "users_num": 2
    },
    {
      "tweet_bucket": 2,
      "users_num": 1
    }
  ],
  "reference_sql": "WITH user_tweets AS (\n  SELECT user_id, COUNT(tweet_id) AS tweet_count\n  FROM tweets\n  WHERE YEAR(tweet_date) = 2022\n  GROUP BY user_id\n)\nSELECT tweet_count AS tweet_bucket, COUNT(user_id) AS users_num\nFROM user_tweets\nGROUP BY tweet_count\nORDER BY tweet_bucket;",
